 "summary": {
  "version": 2,
  "basis": "em",
  "attribution": "Written by a model from the explanatory memorandum; not the record",
  "describes_version": "original",
  "as_of": "2024-03-20",
  "sentences": [
   "The bill would amend the Customs Tariff Act 1995 to raise customs duty on imported tobacco products, giving legislative effect to the Customs Tariff Proposal (No. 2) 2023 tabled on 7 August 2023.",
   "It would increase the customs duty rate for all tobacco products by five per cent a year for three years from 1 September 2023, on top of existing biannual indexation to average weekly ordinary time earnings.",
   "The amendments would apply retrospectively from 1 September 2023, and the bill sits with the Excise Tariff Amendment (Tobacco) Bill 2024, which would make matching changes for tobacco manufactured in Australia."
  ],
  "changes": [
   "The weight conversion factor for tobacco taxed per kilogram, such as loose leaf tobacco, would fall by 0.000025 each year on 1 September from 2023 to 2026, taking it from 0.0007 to 0.0006.",
   "That change would raise the per kilogram duty to broadly align it with the per stick duty on cigarettes.",
   "The higher rate would apply to goods imported on or after 1 September 2023 and to earlier imports where the duty rate had not yet been worked out.",
   "Transitional provisions would treat indexation under the old formula on 1 September 2023 and 1 March 2024 as of no effect and replace it with indexation under the amended formula."
  ],
  "affected": "Tobacco importers and people who buy tobacco products would be affected.",
